<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best World Drop Items for Balance Druids</span></h2>Mists of Pandaria brings with it a whole lot of world content with the chance to drop powerful gear. This will be from World Bosses, such as <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=60491/sha-of-anger">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sha of Anger</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=62346/galleon">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Galleon</span></a>.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="galleon-warbands">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mushanbeastmount.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Galleon and Salyis' Warband</span></h3>Galleon is a World Boss that has a chance to reward players who kill him with ilvl-496 loot. As a Balance Druid, there are 8 different items we want.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90410/cap-of-wandering-pride">
<img alt="Cap of Wandering Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_leather_raiddruid_k_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cap of Wandering Pride</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90419/fireproofed-chestguard">
<img alt="Fireproofed Chestguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fireproofed Chestguard</span></a> - We prefer the helm but will be happy for either. We still want to maintain tier bonuses, so only pick one.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90441/stompdodger-boots">
<img alt="Stompdodger Boots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_leather_raiddruid_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stompdodger Boots</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90450/carrot-holder-belt">
<img alt="Carrot-Holder Belt" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_leather_raiddruid_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carrot-Holder Belt</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90430/stomphowl-pendant">
<img alt="Stomphowl Pendant" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_108.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stomphowl Pendant</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90429/necklace-of-imbued-fury">
<img alt="Necklace of Imbued Fury" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_95.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Necklace of Imbued Fury</span></a> - We prefer Stomphowl Pendant.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90434/steaming-seal-of-flame">
<img alt="Steaming Seal of Flame" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_150.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Steaming Seal of Flame</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90435/ring-of-wretched-flames">
<img alt="Ring of Wretched Flames" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_145.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Wretched Flames</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="sha-of-anger">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/sha_spell_fire_felfirenova.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Sha of Anger</span></h3>Sha of Anger is notable in that it drops ilvl-496 Tier 14 legs and gloves, as well as various ilvl-483 Malevolent Gladiator's pieces. This is a great way to get a head start on your Tier set if you get lucky. <br/>
<br/>The first time you kill the Sha of Anger, it will also drop <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89317/claw-of-anger">
<img alt="Claw of Anger" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_hand_1h_shaclaw.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Claw of Anger</span></a>. This can be turned in for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90908/crushing-treads-of-anger">
<img alt="Crushing Treads of Anger" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_leather_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crushing Treads of Anger</span></a>, a decent early pair of boots.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="oondasta">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_mount_triceratopsmount_blue.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Oondasta</span></h3>Oondasta is a world boss similar to Galleon in that it drops a wide variety of items with item level around that of normal raiding for Tier 15. All of these are upgrades to your pre-BiS and killing Oondasta weekly gives a nice chance at an upgrade!<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95181/amulet-of-the-titanorex">
<img alt="Amulet of the Titanorex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_127.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Amulet of the Titanorex</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95177/choker-of-stygimolochy">
<img alt="Choker of Stygimolochy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_124.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Choker of Stygimolochy</span></a> - We prefer Titanorex for having Crit but it should be a very minor difference.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95186/belt-of-crushed-dreams">
<img alt="Belt of Crushed Dreams" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Crushed Dreams</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95147/fancifully-frilled-tunic">
<img alt="Fancifully Frilled Tunic" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fancifully Frilled Tunic</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95195/gloves-of-unliving-fossil">
<img alt="Gloves of Unliving Fossil" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_leather_raiddruid_m_01glove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of Unliving Fossil</span></a> - The chest is a bit better, they are very comparable and either is fine. We don't want both as that would prevent us from maintaining 4set Tier bonus.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95164/eye-of-oondasta">
<img alt="Eye of Oondasta" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_45.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eye of Oondasta</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95163/ring-of-shamuru">
<img alt="Ring of Shamuru" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_174.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Shamuru</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="nalak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_pandarenserpentmount_lightning_blue.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Nalak</span></h3>Nalak is the Sha of Anger for Tier 15, dropping Tier legs and gloves, as well as PvP gear and a chance at a mount. Unlike Sha, he does not have a guaranteed quest item however.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Reputation Items for Balance Druids</span></h2>The reputation gear we are looking for in Phase 3 will mostly be from Shadow-Pan Assault. It has item level comparable to what you find in Normal Mode Throne of Thunder, making it some of the best pre-raid gear for us. Getting past friendly will however take a lot of time or require raiding.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="the-klaxxi">
